    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1127">

                <pb facs="0560" n="1942" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v13p2/pg1942"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.51G/8–1354</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of Defense for International
                        Security Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hensel</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-08-13">August 13, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: In accordance with the
                    informal request of the Department of State, the Joint Chiefs of Staff were
                    requested to consider the draft message to Prime Minister Mendes-France
                    regarding United States policy toward Indochina. The views of the Joint Chiefs
                    of Staff have been received and a copy is attached. These views <pb facs="0561"
                        n="1943" xml:id="pg1943"/> are consistent with their views regarding United
                    States assumption of training responsibilities in Indochina which were forwarded
                    to you with the concurrence of the Secretary of Defense on 11 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">12</hi>] August.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1127-f1"/></p>
                <p>This Department fully concurs in the attached views and recommendations of the
                    Joint Chiefs of Staff, except that it will not be necessary for the Joint Chiefs
                    of Staff to review the proposed message after it has been amended to reflect the
                    recommendations in paragraph 5 of their comments.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Struve Hensel</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d1127-a1.xml" xpointer="d1127-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
